(5083040, 739626, 100849, '<td valign="top">wow! this is simply fantastic</td>', 'wow! this is simply fantastic', '2008-11-25 03:12:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5083041, 739681, 37858, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and the "peer" award from chromeydome.  The subject is the remnant of a leaf at the base of a plant.  I thought about cropping the photo and even about using the rule of thirds to put it off-center.  I decided against cropping because the photo is as much about darkness as "heart" and I couldn''t see cropping out the darkness for the sake of a "rule" of photography.  I also didn''t like the idea of an off-center composition because a "heart" generally is at the center of things. So there you have it.<br/> <br/>I am pleased that some people appreciated the photo.  I never expect everyone to appreciate anything I do.  All comments, however, are always welcome.  Feedback is a beautiful thing, even where I disagree with the content of the comments.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments and the "peer" award from chromeydome.  The subject is the remnant of a leaf at the base of a plant.  I thought about cropping the photo and even about using the rule of thirds to put it off-center.  I decided against cropping because the photo is as much about darkness as "heart" and I couldn''t see cropping out the darkness for the sake of a "rule" of photography.  I also didn''t like the idea of an off-center composition because a "heart" generally is at the center of things. So there you have it. I am pleased that some people appreciated the photo.  I never expect everyone to appreciate anything I do.  All comments, however, are always welcome.  Feedback is a beautiful thing, even where I disagree with the content of the comments.', '2008-11-25 03:13:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5083389, 739634, 70265, '<td valign="top">Hi Shez, We have a museum here in the U.S. in Sanibel Island, Florida called the Bailey-Matthews Shell Museum. There is collection there of "Sailors'' Valentines" that your art really reminds me of. Have you ever heard of this art form? They are quite unique and beautiful, and the photos don''t even do them justice.<br/> <br/>Take a peek ....<br/> <br/>//www.shellmuseum.org/Map/sailor.htm</td>', 'Hi Shez, We have a museum here in the U.S. in Sanibel Island, Florida called the Bailey-Matthews Shell Museum. There is collection there of "Sailors'' Valentines" that your art really reminds me of. Have you ever heard of this art form? They are quite unique and beautiful, and the photos don''t even do them justice. Take a peek .... //www.shellmuseum.org/Map/sailor.htm', '2008-11-25 11:16:55.000000', NULL, 0),
