(5084012, 739681, 82985, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by chalice:</b></div><hr/><i>  I couldn''t see cropping out the darkness for the sake of a "rule" of photography.  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Every time I see someone invoke or cite the "RULE" of Thirds, I cringe a little.  Especially when they say the "rule" has been "violated"<br/> <br/>At most, it is a tool that <i>may </i>be use in the composition of <i>some</i> images, where appropriate...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-25 19:02:02.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by chalice:  I couldn''t see cropping out the darkness for the sake of a "rule" of photography.    Every time I see someone invoke or cite the "RULE" of Thirds, I cringe a little.  Especially when they say the "rule" has been "violated" At most, it is a tool that may be use in the composition of some images, where appropriate...', '2008-11-25 19:00:30.000000', '2008-11-25 19:02:02.000000', 0),
